        "facts": ["Danto developed the idea of the artworld after Warhol's Brillo Box.", "Brillo Box looked almost exactly like ordinary boxes.", "Dickie defined art as an artifact presented to an artworld public.", "Critics call the theory circular and elitist."],
        "misconceptions": ["The institutional theory says critics may call anything art for any reason.", "If art depends on context, it cannot be good or bad."] },
      { "key": "open-concept", "title": "Judge whether art can be defined", "description": "Argues whether art has an essence or is an open, family-resemblance concept.",
