        "facts": ["The Impressionists relied on dealers such as Paul Durand-Ruel.", "Rejection by the Salon could cost buyers and reputation.", "Independent exhibitions required funds and organization.", "A strong answer asks whether market pressure replaced academic pressure."],
        "misconceptions": ["Leaving the Salon meant artists were free of all outside pressure.", "Commercial success shows a movement was never radical."] }
